WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.980
Good morning, John. It is Wednesday, April 28th 2010.

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:08.280
Welcome to April 28th. What is it? What... what is April 28th, really?

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.340
I just looked it up.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:11.500
It's administrative professionals day.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.800
Administrative professionals out there, you guys. Thank you so much.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:18.640
I don't have any idea what you do, but you administrate.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:20.860
You are pros...

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:21.440
at it.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:24.240
It is also... national poetry reading day.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.100
And I can definitely get on board with that.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.160
Here, here's one.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.160
Haikus are easy.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.016
But sometimes they don't make sense.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:31.420
Refrigerator.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.300
Here's another one of my favourites.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.440
I will not play tug-o-war. I'd rather play hug-o-war.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:38.320
Where everyone hugs instead of tugs,

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:40.460
where everyone giggles and rolls on the rug.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:45.033
Where everyone kisses, and everyone grins, and everyone cuddles and everyone wins.

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:47.260
I like poetry that doesn't confuse me.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:49.500
A lot of poetry, I read it and I'm like...

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:52.960
*noises*

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.120
I hate when poets assume that I know what they mean even when they don't say.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:01.554
But Shel Silverstein, he says what he means, he just says it in a more clever way.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:02.320
I'M A POET!

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:04.320
So back to hugs and rolling on rugs.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:07.573
A little while ago there was a nerdfighter in the comments who said

00:01:07.573 --> 00:01:08.200
something.

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:09.060
Uh, in

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:10.300
the comments.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.720
I don't remember who it was and I'm sorry to that person.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:13.220
But,

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.360
They left a comment saying something about a bucket list of hugs.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:18.160
A bucket list, for those of you who don't know

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:21.120
is a list of things you would like to do before you kick the bucket,

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.360
And for those of you who don't know what kicking the bucket is,

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:26.620
it's a bizarre, American, euphemism for dying.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:30.520
So of course I immediately shortened this sentiment to the "hug bucket".

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:33.340
So your hug bucket is the bucket that all of your hugs go into.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:35.280
And hopefully, we have a lot of them.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.780
And there are certain people, that you want to get inside of your hug bucket.

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:42.620
Like, for example, for me, we got John and John of They Might Be Giants,

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:45.260
Wil Wheaton, David Tennant, Nathan Fillion.

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:47.840
ZeFrank, the Mythbusters, the founders of Threadless,

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:52.620
Felicia Day, Jonathan Coulton, uh, that guy who holds up the "free hugs" sign,

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:54.040
I really wanna hug that guy.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:55.280
Helen Hunt, of course.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:57.680
Kim Stanley Robinson, MC Frontalot.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:58.780
Ursula LeGuinn.

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:00.400
These people, these people that I love.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.840
That I love and I've never met them but I just want to hug them,

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:06.280
because I'm so impressed with the stuff that they do.

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:09.880
And Youtubers! So many Youtubers that I want to hug that I haven't hugged yet.

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:12.880
Which is not to say that my hug bucket is not in a good position,

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:14.260
like I think my hug bucket is,

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:15.540
is a sturdy,

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:18.300
well-formed and quite full hug bucket.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:23.320
Every day I get to add more hugs from the Katherine, and there's no hugs that I would rather have in my hug bucket.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:27.520
There are plenty of hugs from John Green, there's hugs from Alex Day and Charlie McDonald.

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:30.600
There's hugs from Shay Carl, all of my awesome friends and family.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:32.340
All those people in my hug bucket.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:36.320
And let's not kid ourselves, Vidcon is going to be very good for my hug bucket.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:38.020
It's gonna get bigger.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:42.780
Additionally, I am going to add two and a half names from the list that I just mentioned.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.880
In a couple of weeks, not very long from now,

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:48.074
because I am going to be playing W00tstock.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.800
In Portland and Seattle on the 7th and 8th of May.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:56.480
I'm going to get to meet and hang out with Adam Savage, MC Frontalot,

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:58.380
Wil freaking Wheaton,

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:02.120
and a bunch of other, like, epically awesome nerds.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:04.000
And I am going to, without a doubt,

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:07.620
be playing "What Would Captain Picard Do?", in front of Wil Wheaton,

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:10.460
who, in my head, is still Wesley Crusher.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:14.540
Now this geek-and-song fest is definitely PG-13

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:17.140
it might even be PG-15 or 16,

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:22.414
but tickets are available now and you can go to the links in the dooblydoo if you live in Portland or Seattle.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:27.980
And you can see me play a 10 minute set among 3 hours of festival of awesome.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:30.160
But what I wanna know now is who is in your hug bucket?

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:32.980
And don't just say me, because, y'know, I know you wanna hug this.

00:03:32.994 --> 00:03:37.154
Tell me who is in your hug bucket. John, I will see you on Friday.

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:48.360
*delightful hug-related singing*

